r-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543862} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f76cdf7-8c2e-5196-9f1e-b93f95d0b0e2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543847} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29710f27-4a0c-540d-9afb-36c328129c2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543848}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543848} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5baf09d-53ca-5d62-bb06-c003ce6dd6fc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543884}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "81fb6273-5dee-5beb-bfc9-3f4b77ae324c" :question/problem "For the ellipse $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\frac{5}{4}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\frac{27}{4}}=1,\n$$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=\\frac{5}{4}$ and ${b}^{2}=\\frac{27}{4}.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=\\frac{5}{4},$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $$\n\\displaystyle a=\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{4}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}.\n$$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=\\frac{27}{4},$ the length of the vertical radius must be $$\n\\displaystyle b=\\sqrt{\\frac{27}{4}}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $b=\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}=3\\sqrt{3},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}=\\sqrt{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543878 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e7a2f97-cecf-54f4-977c-ad480185865c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$37$ and $\\frac{73}{9}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543863} {:answer/id #uuid "82e1672b-a1cf-5e4f-b7ec-400e71ee5eb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{37}$ and $\\frac{2\\sqrt{73}}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543870} {:answer/id #uuid "b3598dd1-c765-5f19-9a18-ce18efdacfdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{37}$ and $\\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543883} {:answer/id #uuid "cb386ed9-a60a-507f-a0a0-3b956d0d46eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{37}$ and $\\frac{2\\sqrt{73}}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543889} {:answer/id #uuid "d4ab06df-aa62-554d-b1a3-91a2d87f977e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{37}$ and $\\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543893}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543870} :answer-field/id #uuid "db39f157-86de-5b5e-aa65-9e3ecfdb909d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a8e4213c-472e-5df6-a92b-8b65321f34cc" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{{x}^{2}}{37}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\frac{73}{9}}=1?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=37$ and ${b}^{2}=\\frac{73}{9}.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=37,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{37}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=\\frac{73}{9},$ the length of the vertical radius must be $$\n\\displaystyle b=\\sqrt{\\frac{73}{9}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{3}.\n$$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=\\sqrt{37},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{37}=2\\sqrt{37},$ and the minor axis has length $$\n\\displaystyle 2b=2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{3}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{73}}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543886 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0005c1d8-45ea-525d-a5f3-270652f70c50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{53}$ and $\\sqrt{13}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543843} {:answer/id #uuid "346354a8-96ab-5ac3-afa2-7e1332833460" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{53}$ and $\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543850} {:answer/id #uuid "3b9750c6-a897-50af-bf8f-f7809c90a66d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$53$ and $\\frac{13}{4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543854} {:answer/id #uuid "40f0a89a-ba5c-5eb5-a4c7-9438df455d0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{53}$ and $\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543856} {:answer/id #uuid "a21ae6c2-3d2e-5bd5-bda8-5f05bc8b8bc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{53}$ and $\\sqrt{13}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543877}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543843} :answer-field/id #uuid "73b86f1d-d066-5db0-a46a-9f0d01c45177" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543865}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c3eafdd8-07a8-5eeb-996a-7c5b2fca35e0" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{{x}^{2}}{53}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\frac{13}{4}}=1?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=53$ and ${b}^{2}=\\frac{13}{4}.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=53,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{53}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=\\frac{13}{4},$ the length of the vertical radius must be $$\n\\displaystyle b=\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{4}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}.\n$$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=\\sqrt{53},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{53}=2\\sqrt{53},$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}=\\sqrt{13}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543896 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac8378fb-e823-5792-b0e8-141ffa012178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{47}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543880}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543880} :answer-field/id #uuid "50ac688e-f2ed-5c1e-b30b-f87af88a4c4e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543857} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4f06786-52b2-5301-9c27-c84a9739b589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543887}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543887} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c7c7107-1beb-5ce0-af4d-c6cb96a01e5b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543873}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d560ab9f-5f69-5c94-a9a1-63ff925308ba" :question/problem "For the ellipse $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\frac{47}{9}}=1,\n$$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=16$ and ${b}^{2}=\\frac{47}{9}.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=16,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{16}=4.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=\\frac{47}{9},$ the length of the vertical radius must be $$\n\\displaystyle b=\\sqrt{\\frac{47}{9}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{47}}{3}.\n$$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=4,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\frac{\\sqrt{47}}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 4=8,$ and the minor axis has length $$\n\\displaystyle 2b=2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{47}}{3}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{47}}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543898 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6418b296-10d2-5b35-b945-05b31aba2d9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{17}$ and $\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543861} {:answer/id #uuid "90328bb5-2efb-5b62-9495-b0a760fef10a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$17$ and $\\frac{13}{4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543874} {:answer/id #uuid "d3bb7b1f-836e-5b98-9cdd-890c7f95b0ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{17}$ and $\\sqrt{13}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543892} {:answer/id #uuid "d502494b-1775-539d-9e06-67be767210e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{17}$ and $\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543895} {:answer/id #uuid "f7023301-1a20-54bd-92af-1b064d386811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{17}$ and $\\sqrt{13}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543902}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543902} :answer-field/id #uuid "7347b547-af23-57b6-bf2a-d08e54524091" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543864}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e487ead8-2208-53bd-a890-504c42fca111" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\frac{13}{4}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{17}=1?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=\\frac{13}{4}$ and ${b}^{2}=17.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=\\frac{13}{4},$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $$\n\\displaystyle a=\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{4}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}.\n$$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=17,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{17}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=\\sqrt{17},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{17}=2\\sqrt{17},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}=\\sqrt{13}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546025 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b11bbd0f-79e3-5617-9dc5-99fa2d76e8bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4 e^{- x - 5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546057}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546057} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd651fe4-1b43-5b99-8d28-0d5282dfb011" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546070}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "05c06d18-760a-55d8-8f2d-5ce452eb9a43" :question/problem "Given that $y=-4{e}^{-5-x},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=-4{e}^{u},\\,u=-5-x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-4{e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-1.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-4{e}^{u}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =4{e}^{u} \\\\  & =4{e}^{-5-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546033 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7367a804-a6e2-5743-81c8-c134ab3e3d40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5 x^{4} + 5 e^{4 - 5 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546044}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546044} :answer-field/id #uuid "05118342-1d20-597e-be23-0e46a68395ca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546024}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3b4c3b4f-ee6c-5156-ab65-2225d5039897" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{'}(x)$ if $f(x)={x}^{5}-{e}^{4-5x}.$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y={e}^{4-5x}$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={e}^{u},\\,u=4-5x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}={e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-5.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-5{e}^{u} \\\\  & =-5{e}^{4-5x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the sum rule of differentiation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{5}-{e}^{4-5x}) \\\\  & =5{x}^{4}-(-5{e}^{4-5x}) \\\\  & =5({x}^{4}+{e}^{4-5x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546037 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5884aa2-d5ab-5f93-8897-89214c01b41a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4 e^{4 x - 6} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546074}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546074} :answer-field/id #uuid "0222a237-315c-536e-ad55-3c45f766115e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546023}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "46c70445-c7fa-5e96-b9db-24423c65d9d2" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)=2x+{e}^{4x-6}.$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y={e}^{4x-6}$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={e}^{u},\\,u=4x-6.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}={e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =4{e}^{u} \\\\  & =4{e}^{4x-6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the sum rule of differentiation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x+{e}^{4x-6}) \\\\  & =2+4{e}^{4x-6} \\\\  & =4{e}^{4x-6}+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546039 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06f3b1be-7698-59e3-aef0-38dd300bf844" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 12 e x + 6 + 3 e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546026} {:answer/id #uuid "15a35f43-a4b7-584e-b180-d26a6e86a916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 12 e \\left(x + \\frac{7}{4}\\right) + 3 e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546028} {:answer/id #uuid "631a33cb-a6bf-5512-a0f9-90d28f159483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 12 e x - 18 e + 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546042} {:answer/id #uuid "a9fdf460-843a-56b3-b956-5712f66fb700" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=3 e \\left(x + \\frac{7}{4}\\right) + 6 + 3 e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546055} {:answer/id #uuid "d18d0448-5ee2-554a-b226-5c667ed7dbe9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=12 e \\left(x + \\frac{7}{4}\\right) + 6 + 3 e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546064}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546042} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7fdb164-208e-53f2-a5fb-7d65ea9753b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "52a84e58-ee14-59cb-b2fc-5dc806f58a59" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=3{e}^{-4x-6}+6$ at the point where $x=- \\frac{7}{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=3{e}^{u}+6,\\,u=-4x-6.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=3{e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =3{e}^{u}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-12{e}^{u} \\\\  & =-12{e}^{-4x-6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the slope of the tangent to the curve at $x=- \\frac{7}{4}$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=- \\frac{7}{4}} & =-12{e}^{-4x-6}{|}_{x=- \\frac{7}{4}} \\\\ & =-12{e}^{(-4)\\left(- \\frac{7}{4}\\right)-6} \\\\ & =- 12 e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, the $y$-value of the point on the curve where $x=x_1=- \\frac{7}{4}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y_1 & =(3{e}^{-4x-6}+6){|}_{x=- \\frac{7}{4}} \\\\ & =3{e}^{(-4)\\left(- \\frac{7}{4}\\right)-6}+6 \\\\ & =6 + 3 e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1 & =m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(6 + 3 e) & =(- 12 e)(x-\\left(- \\frac{7}{4}\\right)) \\\\ y-(6 + 3 e) & =- 12 e x-(21 e) \\\\ y & =- 12 e x - 18 e + 6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546047 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00fd1e00-d8ad-53a1-a4ce-5e09d463daa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 2 e \\left(x - \\frac{1}{3}\\right) - 2 e + 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546022} {:answer/id #uuid "0d3a07ef-c7b6-5bda-8a5f-02f36078cba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=6 e x - 4 e + 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546027} {:answer/id #uuid "386252c4-f73b-5706-99ea-15795c9c3a0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=6 e \\left(x - \\frac{1}{3}\\right) - 2 e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546031} {:answer/id #uuid "9237bc66-6da2-5b5f-af2c-8e5ce3b5744d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 6 e \\left(x - \\frac{1}{3}\\right) - 2 e + 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546049} {:answer/id #uuid "d0bc922d-bb0e-5a70-b6c9-97af108437ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=6 e x - 2 e + 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546063}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546027} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0779349-01a1-5902-a3ac-f744fc1c935b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546056}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7fd12a30-30af-5a77-a4c8-bf313d7546d2" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=-2{e}^{-3x+2}+3$ at the point where $x=\\frac{1}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=-2{e}^{u}+3,\\,u=-3x+2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-2{e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{u}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =6{e}^{u} \\\\  & =6{e}^{-3x+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the slope of the tangent to the curve at $x=\\frac{1}{3}$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=\\frac{1}{3}} & =6{e}^{-3x+2}{|}_{x=\\frac{1}{3}} \\\\ & =6{e}^{(-3)\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)+2} \\\\ & =6 e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, the $y$-value of the point on the curve where $x=x_1=\\frac{1}{3}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y_1 & =(-2{e}^{-3x+2}+3){|}_{x=\\frac{1}{3}} \\\\ & =-2{e}^{(-3)\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)+2}+3 \\\\ & =3 - 2 e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1 & =m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(3 - 2 e) & =(6 e)(x-\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)) \\\\ y-(3 - 2 e) & =6 e x-(2 e) \\\\ y & =6 e x - 4 e + 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546052 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e2c2b01-8349-508f-bf8e-50f3ae9bc58a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 4 e^{- 4 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546029} {:answer/id #uuid "5c1ee9ed-13be-5d25-80da-1864c503d155" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{- 4 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546041} {:answer/id #uuid "944f0d6a-3b60-545c-b2e8-97b3032ade29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x e^{- 4 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546050} {:answer/id #uuid "d7f84086-3f8f-549a-8676-8413302b70c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{e^{- 4 x}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546067} {:answer/id #uuid "f21accce-80c4-5fb5-9b8e-0ed03436a5cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 4 x e^{- 4 x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546078}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546029} :answer-field/id #uuid "31ba4f18-563e-5f43-91f8-a07770c36c56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9f144a62-dd63-5191-a104-7945db3746f9" :question/problem "Given that $f(x) = e^{-4x}$, find $\\frac{df}{dx}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={e}^{u},\\,u=-4x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}={e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-4{e}^{u} \\\\  & =-4{e}^{-4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546058 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b20bc36-ce98-5edb-9e51-7375356be643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 30 e \\left(x - \\frac{5}{6}\\right) + 1 + 5 e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546032} {:answer/id #uuid "3bfaf069-a4d6-5131-a87d-a208594f2c61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=30 e x + 1 + 5 e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546034} {:answer/id #uuid "72048a0c-73ca-54b2-aa19-72248fb1e5b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=5 e \\left(x - \\frac{5}{6}\\right) + 1 + 5 e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546043} {:answer/id #uuid "750cf673-67dd-5803-97c5-520a46254372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=30 e \\left(x - \\frac{5}{6}\\right) + 5 e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546045} {:answer/id #uuid "eb9790a2-417d-5f52-a1e3-b34bb0797907" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=30 e x - 20 e + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546077}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546077} :answer-field/id #uuid "4506d1a2-b6f8-5a68-becb-87dba57a7620" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546036}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b32ededd-4f82-5701-b090-5a6b3fd40512" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=5{e}^{6x-4}+1$ at the point where $x=\\frac{5}{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=5{e}^{u}+1,\\,u=6x-4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=5{e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =5{e}^{u}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =30{e}^{u} \\\\  & =30{e}^{6x-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the slope of the tangent to the curve at $x=\\frac{5}{6}$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=\\frac{5}{6}} & =30{e}^{6x-4}{|}_{x=\\frac{5}{6}} \\\\ & =30{e}^{(6)\\left(\\frac{5}{6}\\right)-4} \\\\ & =30 e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, the $y$-value of the point on the curve where $x=x_1=\\frac{5}{6}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y_1 & =(5{e}^{6x-4}+1){|}_{x=\\frac{5}{6}} \\\\ & =5{e}^{(6)\\left(\\frac{5}{6}\\right)-4}+1 \\\\ & =1 + 5 e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1 & =m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(1 + 5 e) & =(30 e)(x-\\left(\\frac{5}{6}\\right)) \\\\ y-(1 + 5 e) & =30 e x-(25 e) \\\\ y & =30 e x - 20 e + 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546062 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4401eafb-fa33-5c95-b049-85b630f2f47d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 12 e x - 4 e - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546035} {:answer/id #uuid "97abff75-225b-5630-aa11-86faced36582" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=12 e \\left(x - 2\\right) - 4 e - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546051} {:answer/id #uuid "bffd7f70-58d6-5df1-9b3d-3f23c0d090b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 12 e x - 3 + 20 e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546060} {:answer/id #uuid "d3230802-1784-5568-9bac-fcc769b517fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 12 e \\left(x - 2\\right) - 4 e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546065} {:answer/id #uuid "e5850b7d-6ef6-55a7-b9dc-7cf2a4da7531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 4 e \\left(x - 2\\right) - 4 e - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546073}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546060} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0fece4a-a8bb-548d-abc6-f90d6ed2350c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546061}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c6bcf79b-eac1-52f9-ad10-1945c83effb0" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=-4{e}^{3x-5}-3$ at the point where $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=-4{e}^{u}-3,\\,u=3x-5.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-4{e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-4{e}^{u}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-12{e}^{u} \\\\  & =-12{e}^{3x-5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the slope of the tangent to the curve at $x=2$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=2} & =-12{e}^{3x-5}{|}_{x=2} \\\\ & =-12{e}^{(3)(2)-5} \\\\ & =- 12 e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, the $y$-value of the point on the curve where $x=x_1=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y_1 & =(-4{e}^{3x-5}-3){|}_{x=2} \\\\ & =-4{e}^{(3)(2)-5}-3 \\\\ & =- 4 e - 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1 & =m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(- 4 e - 3) & =(- 12 e)(x-(2)) \\\\ y-(- 4 e - 3) & =- 12 e x-(- 24 e) \\\\ y & =- 12 e x - 3 + 20 e.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546066 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c3f86e4-f000-591a-af10-3b0f2e76f24a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 2 e \\left(x - 3\\right) - 2 e - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546046} {:answer/id #uuid "a136be05-5ae5-5cba-ba24-898cc2845c42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=4 e \\left(x - 3\\right) - 2 e - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546053} {:answer/id #uuid "b98c737b-5fe4-5f99-b515-19aeda98c743" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 4 e x - 2 e - 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546059} {:answer/id #uuid "dbf426b4-1cd9-558c-9feb-975ace11ad79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 4 e x - 3 + 10 e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546069} {:answer/id #uuid "fe9ac606-867e-5fe4-86a8-ece4d77edd4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=- 4 e \\left(x - 3\\right) - 2 e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546079}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546069} :answer-field/id #uuid "df16da41-2070-5b0b-a923-30c6662c499b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546071}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d323abf4-feef-5783-8c9c-89b3cff14f40" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=-2{e}^{2x-5}-3$ at the point where $x=3.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=-2{e}^{u}-3,\\,u=2x-5.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-2{e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{u}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-4{e}^{u} \\\\  & =-4{e}^{2x-5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the slope of the tangent to the curve at $x=3$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=3} & =-4{e}^{2x-5}{|}_{x=3} \\\\ & =-4{e}^{(2)(3)-5} \\\\ & =- 4 e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, the $y$-value of the point on the curve where $x=x_1=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y_1 & =(-2{e}^{2x-5}-3){|}_{x=3} \\\\ & =-2{e}^{(2)(3)-5}-3 \\\\ & =- 2 e - 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1 & =m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(- 2 e - 3) & =(- 4 e)(x-(3)) \\\\ y-(- 2 e - 3) & =- 4 e x-(- 12 e) \\\\ y & =- 4 e x - 3 + 10 e.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546072 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f3504cb-45f2-555b-80a1-81a0a0f42939" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\left(4 x + 7\\right) e^{4 x + 7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546038} {:answer/id #uuid "576283f7-d522-5cbc-8f21-65c4b15b8858" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4 x e^{4 x + 7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546040} {:answer/id #uuid "8fe2cbd2-f59b-5b92-9bbb-c00d3642dbdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{4 x + 7}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546048} {:answer/id #uuid "a34e7884-71c6-53d5-84dd-7dca5dc3d217" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{4 x + 7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546054} {:answer/id #uuid "e7c99c8a-3c47-5367-bb23-9f844b5ea84a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4 e^{4 x + 7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546075}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186546075} :answer-field/id #uuid "d88ed9d7-c7fa-5b42-a090-ad8da7bf1370" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546068}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e1a53e4b-cb95-5fd7-83e2-0c854f6893c1" :question/problem "Given that $f(x) = e^{4x + 7}$, find $\\frac{df}{dx}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={e}^{u},\\,u=4x+7.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}={e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =4{e}^{u} \\\\  & =4{e}^{4x+7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547977 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9f82827-bfc3-518b-84b7-a88995159d91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sin(x^2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547690}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547690} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf767100-f800-58a2-a235-bc232ccd9496" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547947}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "11ed723f-8fe2-5c56-8bb0-841acdfb0940" :question/math-academy-id "q-126766" :question/problem "Given that $|C|\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ use the general solution to the equation to find the function $f(x).$\n\n$f(x)\\,\\,=\\,\\,$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The general solution is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+C).\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=0$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({0}^{2}+C) \\\\ 0 & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(C) \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of ${y}^{′}=xy$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=0$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+0)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}).\n$$\n\nHence, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547982 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d692ba23-e86a-5e24-a39c-8c7caf6f455f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547772}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547772} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d2156ef-39e9-59d1-b08e-81876504abac" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547878}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1bc80b6f-e02e-58f0-97b4-8ea651af23ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-126765" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation. Express your answer in the form $y=y(x).$\n\n$y\\,\\,=\\,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,C),\\,\\,$where $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "First, we separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y & ={x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a perfectly valid general solution. However, if we want to write $y=y(x)$ explicitly, then we can solve for $y.$ This gives\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+C)\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550328 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49b27fdd-cc9a-5801-b180-01f4a70bc0bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{169}+\\frac{16{y}^{2}}{529}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550332}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550332} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0e1ae4d-133e-5ac3-84d6-bc430526f02a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550341}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1a6b38d4-7f97-5b59-aaba-751584b345ee" :question/problem "![](images/5e/5e9a8c7db3d0a811ca1dc95db8060a5488b4b9b2fb47fc08d25f1a959357626e.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{13}{3}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{23}{4}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{\\left(\\frac{13}{3}\\right)}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{\\left(\\frac{23}{4}\\right)}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\left(\\frac{169}{9}\\right)}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\left(\\frac{529}{16}\\right)} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{9{x}^{2}}{169}+\\frac{16{y}^{2}}{529} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
